Sval: mozlog prints minidump-stackwalk's stack along with its stderr

Backport of Mozilla's Bug 2065184 (mozilla-central 62cf9d6795cc, Firefox
156), unchanged. ESR 153 does not carry it.
mozlog's mach and TBPL formatters printed a crash's stackwalk stdout only
when it wrote nothing to stderr, so one benign warning from
minidump-stackwalk dropped the crash's stack from the test log.
Drop this patch when the upstream pin reaches Firefox 156.

diff --git a/testing/mozbase/mozlog/mozlog/formatters/machformatter.py b/testing/mozbase/mozlog/mozlog/formatters/machformatter.py
index 148c72efa6..6ee867201c 100644
--- a/testing/mozbase/mozlog/mozlog/formatters/machformatter.py
+++ b/testing/mozbase/mozlog/mozlog/formatters/machformatter.py
@@ -555,11 +555,11 @@ class MachFormatter(base.BaseFormatter):
                     % data["stackwalk_returncode"]
                 )
 
+            if data.get("stackwalk_stdout"):
+                rv.append(data["stackwalk_stdout"])
             if data.get("stackwalk_stderr"):
                 rv.append("stderr from minidump-stackwalk:")
                 rv.append(data["stackwalk_stderr"])
-            elif data.get("stackwalk_stdout"):
-                rv.append(data["stackwalk_stdout"])
 
             if data.get("stackwalk_errors"):
                 rv.extend(data.get("stackwalk_errors"))
